      "narration": "Mira Thorne extracts a pair of worn leather boots from one of her many pockets and extends them toward Nicco, her plant-stained fingers curling away once he takes them. She says nothing, watching him with the same skeptical, observant manner she might apply to an unfamiliar herb. The boots are plainly made, serviceable, neither new nor fine.\n\nThe square around them holds its moderate daytime traffic, low buildings pressing in with their ordinary lives, and the dark front of The Coined Lie somewhere nearby offering its particular hospitality. Mira stands with her layered, pocketed clothes unchanged, having shed only the weight of boots she clearly did not need.",
